course: dictionary
lesson: 11038
title: Weapon: a thing to attack or win with
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A weapon is something used to hurt or attack, or to defend yourself in a fight. A sword, a spear and a bow with arrows are all weapons. Read the words around it to check: «Rat had his belt bulging with weapons» tells you he was carrying things to fight with.
explain: Weapon has a second meaning too. «Her smile was her secret weapon» does not mean a smile is a real weapon. It means her smile helped her win. The words around it, like secret and her, give you the clue.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Germs come in different kinds, so each needs the right weapon» means each germ needs the right way to fight it. If your meaning makes sense, you have it.
fact: A weapon is something used to hurt, attack or defend in a fight.
fact: «Weapon» can also mean anything used to win against something, as in «her smile was her secret weapon».
fact: The plural of weapon is weapons: one weapon, two weapons.
fact: Animals have natural weapons, such as teeth, claws and stings.
fact: Real weapons are dangerous. If you find one, do not touch it, move away and tell an adult.
exercise: «Rat had his belt bulging with weapons.» What does weapons mean here? | *Things used to attack or defend in a fight | Books full of pictures | Hats worn on a cold day | Ropes used to tie up parcels
exercise: Lena says her smile was her secret weapon. What does she mean? | Her smile was a real gun | She smiled at a shop that sells weapons | Her smile was very sharp | *Her smile helped her win
exercise: Which of these is a natural weapon? | A pillow | *A wasp's sting | A bowl of soup | A sunny window
test: Ben finds a knife in the park. What should he do? | Try it on a tree | Pick it up to show his friends | *Move away and tell an adult | Hide it in his bag
test: What is the plural of weapon? | weaponed | *weapons | weaponry | weapon's
exam: Which sentence uses weapon to mean something that helps you win? | The knight wore a heavy metal helmet. | Ali found an old sword in the museum. | *Mia's kindness was her weapon in the argument. | Dogs have soft fur on their backs.
